## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical concurrency control with per-key ordering and degradation strategies under load.

## Key Concepts
- Bounded queues and backpressure mechanisms
- Per-room FIFO semantics and ordering guarantees
- Fair scheduling across multiple rooms
- Graceful degradation when overwhelmed

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for event dispatcher
while (true) {
  for (room of roundRobinSchedule()) {
    if (room.buffer.hasEvents() && globalQueue.notFull()) {
      globalQueue.enqueue(room.buffer.dequeue());
    } else if (globalQueue.isFull()) {
      applyBackpressure();
    }
  }
}
```

## Test Plan
1. **Per-room ordering**: Send concurrent events to same room, verify FIFO processing
2. **Degradation behavior**: Flood system to trigger threshold, verify non-critical events are dropped/debounced
3. **Graceful shutdown**: Stop accepting new events, process remaining queue, verify no data loss

